      "summaries": {
        "en": "Strix is an open-source AI-powered penetration testing framework that automates vulnerability discovery in applications, addressing the challenge of manual security audits. It employs LLM-driven agents that simulate hacker behaviors to systematically identify weaknesses like SQL injection and XSS. Developers can integrate it into CI/CD pipelines for continuous security testing, or security teams can use it to augment manual penetration testing with automated scanning capabilities.",
        "zh": "Strix是一个开源AI驱动的渗透测试框架，通过自动化漏洞发现解决人工安全审计的挑战。它利用LLM驱动的智能体模拟黑客行为，系统性地识别SQL注入、跨站脚本等常见漏洞。技术核心在于将安全测试任务分解为可执行的代理动作，使大语言模型能够像安全专家一样思考攻击路径。开发者可将其集成到CI/CD流程中实现持续安全测试，安全团队则可用它辅助人工渗透测试，快速扫描应用弱点并生成修复建议。",
        "es": "Strix is an open-source AI-powered penetration testing framework that automates vulnerability discovery in applications, addressing the challenge of manual security audits. It employs LLM-driven agents that simulate hacker behaviors to systematically identify weaknesses like SQL injection and XSS. Developers can integrate it into CI/CD pipelines for continuous security testing, or security teams can use it to augment manual penetration testing with automated scanning capabilities.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "strix stands out for agents, artificial-intelligence, and cybersecurity in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Strix is an open-source AI-powered penetration testing framework that automates vulnerability discovery in applications, addressing the challenge of manual security audits. It employs LLM-driven agents that simulate hacker behaviors to systematically identify weaknesses like SQL injection and XSS. Developers can integrate it into CI/CD pipelines for continuous security testing, or security teams can use it to augment manual penetration testing with automated scanning capabilities.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/usestrix/strix for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
